{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #983: declared status 'open'. Formalized: no. Let $n\\geq 2$ and $\\pi(n)<k\\leq n$. Let $f(k,n)$ be the smallest integer $r$ such that in any $A\\subseteq \\{1,\\ldots,n\\}$ of size $\\lvert A\\rvert=k$ there exist primes $p_1,\\ldots,p_r$ such that at least $r$ many $a\\in A$ are only divisible by primes from $\\{p_1,\\ldots,p_r\\}$.\n\nIs it true that\\[2\\pi(n^{1/2})-f(\\pi(n)+1,n)\\to \\infty\\]as $n\\to \\infty$?\n\nIn general, estimate $f(k,n)$, particularly when $\\pi(n)+1<k=o(n)$. Prize: no. Tags: number theory."},"claim_id":"vcl_09adf949ca6d4070c62312e8211042ca55bef141f53b00adb249e3d597374628","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:983","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_882b09f5cba72e80","object_root":"sha256:2760e1acfc666b922d37352fce70533643602453193f488d8a1eee0dbbee4cf6","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:983"}],"relations":[],"revision":1,"schema":"vela.claim